hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to an  edition of ask Evan today Mason a  question from one of our newsletter  readers male khoa who wrote in asking  can you please give me some information  on why entrepreneurs fail great question  thank you for answer for asking it so  many entrepreneurs fail something like  eighty percent of entrepreneurs fail  within the first five years and there's  a number of reason why that happens and  hopefully I can shed some light on it so  the first one is a lot of entrepreneurs  get into business for the wrong reason  so they get into mrs. just trying to  make money and that's great we want to  make money but it shouldn't be your main  reason for becoming an entrepreneur if  you look at any famous entrepreneur and  if you look on our website with the  largest collection of famous  entrepreneur stories these guys started  because they want to make a difference  they wanted to help people do want to  have an impact and it sounds may be very  fluffy but it's true you know you got to  have a strong passion for what you're  doing you got to really love the  business that you're in because it's so  hard it's it's brutally tough being an  entrepreneur and most people will give  up because they don't love what they're  doing and a lot of these entrepreneurs  the successful ones they would do what  they're doing even if they weren't  getting paid for because they love it so  much so that's what you have to first of  all find something you love so much you  would do it to help people and you do it  even you weren't getting paid for it  because you have that strong passion for  so if you haven't found it yet don't  settle you know keep looking for it  don't give up on on having that great  business idea don't just jump into  something because you think you're going  to make a lot of money and typically  you'll find that money will motivate you  only for so long when you don't see the  results coming in and you really hate  what you're doing every day you're not  going to keep at it you know what it's  too hard and so you're going to quit so  step number one is finding something  you're really strongly passionately in  the deepest part of your soul believe in  and you know you're helping people  because that energizes you right when  you find people writing in to you saying  you change their life or thank you so  much for that that  information or that product of that  service it made a huge impact on me that  motivates you to keep going at least it  does for me and so it ends up giving you  the energy you need to get up every day  and do it all over again and so you  really want to love what you're doing  and there's going to be parts of running  the business that suck even as you grow  and build beyond yourself and have a  team to help you with some of the  admin's stuff there's still parts that  suck but hopefully it sucks less but as  you are able to grow your business and  build it more and more around the things  you're really good at it really love  doing so I would say the number one  reason why entrepreneurs will fails  because they picked a business that  they're not super passionate about and  they're not helping people in so that'd  be the first place i would start the  next reason i would say a lot of  entrepreneurs fail is they quit too soon  they don't allow momentum to build and  running the business is really hard you  know it's hard to get up every day and  do something and not see results and  want results so badly you know as  entrepreneurs we we want things that  happen yesterday we feel so motivated  such at the beginning to get this thing  going and change our lives and be our  own boss that it's frustrating when the  results don't come in quickly but the  reality is a lot of this stuff takes  time to build you know it takes time for  the awareness to get out there it takes  time for the only referral partners to  talk about you people to discover you  your website to take off it does take  time for things to happen and you need  to do something every day to make sure  that that business is growing and too  many entrepreneurs just quit too soon  you know you don't you don't see the  immediate results and so you give up and  what I would try to encourage you to do  is think about think about the value  that you're trying to help think about  the people you're trying to help and try  to channel that motivation into getting  up every day and doing something to help  them I know it's tough you know I know  when you're not seeing anything come  back and just trying to stick to that  vision it can be really hard but I found  that it does it did help me at least and  still does help me think about the  people you're helping try to visualize  you have helped and the  real benefit that they've gotten by you  being in business and if you weren't  there you know what would they have done  so that's the first one and the second  part is think about the life that you  want to create and what you have to do  to get there you know if you keep doing  just the same thing back at your regular  old job are you going to create the  lifestyle that you want is that really  the life that you want to build the  being able to build in the next 10 20 30  40 50 years upendra how old you are you  know so if you're if you're able to  visualize the lifestyle that you want  and get frustrated enough to say you  know I have to change my situation from  you'll be able to build that lifestyle  that can give you the motivation to get  up and and do the work even when nobody  else maybe believes in you and so I find  that to be very helpful so you got to do  something every day and not quit don't  quit too soon which is a huge reason why  a lot of entrepreneurs fail so the first  part is getting to businesses you're not  passionate excited about it the second  part is because you quit too soon and  the third reason I think why a lot of  entrepreneurs fails they don't they  don't stretch themselves enough to be  successful as an entrepreneur we're all  limited right we all have our own  strengths and weaknesses and we're all  really good at things and we all suck at  other things and to be a successful  entrepreneur you're going to have to  push yourself beyond your comfort zones  you know in our comfort zones we tend to  do the things we like and we're good at  and not necessarily the things we have  to do to grow our businesses and if you  want to achieve success you have to be  able to build that degree of discomfort  I guess and what you do to stretch  yourself and put yourself beyond what  you're comfortable doing because you're  going to have to do that be able to get  your company off the ground and up to  that next level success and when people  ask me even now what I feel is the  biggest hurdle in my business and what  keeps me up at night or what the biggest  problem is with my business is usually  limiting personal beliefs you know you  think you're only so good and so that's  how good you can become and if you think  you're better you'll rise to the  occasion and you'll stretch yourself and  you push yourself to get to that next  step so it's easy to get comfortable in  a certain position for some people it's  making fifty thousand dollars a year  a hundred thousand dollars a year  whatever it is you get comfortable you  stop growing you stop pushing yourself  and and that's fine you know if that's  your goal that's great if you want to  achieve more then you have to push  yourself more and so one of the biggest  things i think for growing entrepreneurs  and something is still to me it happens  all the time the biggest challenges  limiting personal beliefs so you only  think you're so good and so that's how  good you are you know if you think you  deserve better and you take the steps to  create a lifestyle that is where you  want to be then you're going to get  there you know if you think you deserve  better and you really in your 